## Two sub-kinds via routing-keyword

Sandbar's `:mm/Actor` class is single-class with TWO codec routing keywords (`type: ai-actor` and `type: human-actor`).  The class is shared; the routing keyword distinguishes the kind at parse time + lands on the entity via the `:mm.actor/actor-type` slot.

## Composition with other classes

- **`:mm/Context`** — actors `runs-in-context:` context memorials; rules apply to (actor, context) tuples
- **`:mm/Rule`** — rules can subject an actor (`:mm.rule/actor`) — apply only to that actor's actions
- **`:mm/Memory`** — memorials cite their author via `:mm.memory/created-by`

